---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Deterministic Chart Rendering for Regulated Reporting">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section style="padding: 6rem 0 4rem; text-align: center;">
    <div class="container">
      <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        <span class="badge">Private Preview</span>
      </p>
      <h1 style="max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto 1.5rem; font-size: 2.75rem; line-height: 1.15;">
        When your Python pipeline and Go service render the same chart and the output
        drifts — even by one pixel — someone has to explain&nbsp;it.
      </h1>
      <p style="max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto 2.5rem; font-size: 1.125rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
        A deterministic, multi-language chart system that makes every chart change
        provable — so regulated reporting teams spend less time explaining visual
        differences and more time shipping.
      </p>
      <a href="#request-access" class="btn btn-primary" style="font-size: 1rem; padding: 0.75rem 2rem;">
        Request early access
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Static chart preview -->
  <section style="padding: 0 0 4rem;">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 860px;">
      <div class="card" style="padding: 0; overflow: hidden;">
        <img
          src="/preview-chart.svg"
          alt="Line chart showing Monthly Average Temperature for Tokyo and London, rendered as deterministic SVG"
          width="820"
          height="460"
          style="display: block; width: 100%; height: auto;"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <p style="padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem; margin: 0; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-tertiary); border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
          Deterministic SVG output. Same spec, same bytes, Python or Go. Zero runtime dependencies.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pain points -->
  <section class="section" style="background: var(--bg-surface);">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        Three problems regulated teams face with chart infrastructure
      </h2>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem;">
        <div class="card">
          <div style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">01</div>
          <h3>Inconsistent output</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0;">
            The same chart spec produces different bytes depending on the language,
            platform, or even the time of day. Two of five major chart libraries embed
            random IDs in their SVG output, making byte-level comparison impossible.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">02</div>
          <h3>Unauditable changes</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0;">
            When a chart in a quarterly filing looks different from the previous version,
            there is no evidence trail showing whether the data changed, the renderer
            changed, or both. The investigation is manual, and the cost is real.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">03</div>
          <h3>Dependency risk</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0;">
            Server-side chart rendering typically requires headless browsers,
            hundreds of npm dependencies, and large memory footprints. One popular
            export server ships 261 dependencies and needs 550 MB of RAM to start.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 720px; text-align: center;">
      <h2 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">A different approach</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        One shared specification. Certified renderers in Python and Go with zero runtime
        dependencies. A conformance tool that proves cross-runtime parity for every release.
      </p>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; text-align: center;">
        <div>
          <div style="font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent);">0</div>
          <div style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">Runtime dependencies</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style="font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent);">2</div>
          <div style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">Certified languages</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style="font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent);">Byte-identical</div>
          <div style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">Cross-runtime output</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Access request -->
  <section id="request-access" class="section" style="background: var(--bg-surface);">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 560px; text-align: center;">
      <h2 style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Request early access</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        The interactive demo includes a chart gallery with six certified chart types,
        measured benchmark comparisons against five chart libraries, and a conformance
        proof showing byte-identical output across Python and Go.
      </p>
      <form id="access-form" style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; max-width: 420px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <input
          type="email"
          name="email"
          placeholder="you@company.com"
          required
          style="flex: 1; padding: 0.625rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); font-size: 0.875rem; background: var(--bg-surface-raised); color: var(--text);"
        />
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Request</button>
      </form>
      <p style="margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-tertiary);">
        We will review requests and grant access within one business day.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 2rem 0; text-align: center;">
    <div class="container" style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-tertiary);">
      Copyright 2026. All rights reserved. This product is in private preview.
    </div>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>
